@@Finding Goldilocks step size and iteration amount@@
@@Remember that Max iterations is too clean, but 40 worked well. Now try going up from lowest iterations@@

@@Try 8 iterations? Evenly spaced steps@@
@@Review: too few, and somehow only got half the box, not the right cylinder, but CAN see left cyl!!! If you look below at 16, it gets left and right!!!@@
#title: B-scan from a metal cylinder buried in a dielectric half-space

#domain: 0.240 0.210 0.002
#dx_dy_dz: 0.002 0.002 0.002
#time_window: 6e-9
/#time_window: 3e-9

#material: 6 0 1 0 half_space
^remember this is in half space!!!!!!! so slower vp

#waveform: ricker 1 1.5e9 my_ricker
#hertzian_dipole: z 0.040 0.170 0 my_ricker
#rx: 0.080 0.170 0

/#src_steps: 0.002 0 0
/#rx_steps: 0.002 0 0
/#rx_steps: 0.004 0 0
^testing steps 2x as big with only 25 iterations (why are we doing 40 iterations though we doubled steps? Maybe try doing 30, since .24/.002=120 and we did 60 iters?!)
/#rx_steps: 0.008 0 0
/^2x as big again!!! do 20 iterations
//#src_steps: 0.080 0 0
//#rx_steps: 0.080 0 0
^biggest possible step size!!
#src_steps: 0.010 0 0
#rx_steps: 0.010 0 0
^trying 8 steps

#box: 0 0 0 0.240 0.170 0.002 half_space
/#cylinder: 0.120 0.080 0 0.120 0.080 0.002 0.010 pec
#cylinder: 0.060 0.080 0 0.060 0.080 0.002 0.010 pec
#cylinder: 0.180 0.080 0 0.180 0.080 0.002 0.010 pec
^if use bottom 2 together, use 40 scans over step of 0.004


/if this is on, when you run python -m tools.outputfiles_merge cylinder_Bscan_2D --remove-file, you still get left with all your .vti's
/only use when visualizing on --geometry-only mode
#geometry_view: 0 0 0 0.240 0.210 0.002 0.002 0.002 0.002 goldilocks_1cm n

To run -n 5 times and get the scan:
python -m gprMax goldilocks_1cm.in -n 8
python -m tools.outputfiles_merge goldilocks_1cm --remove-files
python -m tools.plot_Bscan  goldilocks_1cm_merged.out Ez
